From 19d79a9081ca4c39a3017060e73af00ce5432823 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessio Garzi <agarzi@sipwise.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:15:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] replace TRAUMA-FirstDemo with the relocatable rebuild

The original unpacks itself at the fixed address $30000-$66000 and uses
$70000-$7FFFF for its screens, without allocating any of it. Started
from the menu on a CD32 it worked only if the packed hunk happened to be
loaded below $2FF08: a slightly different boot moved it higher and the
demo crashed (reboot on real hardware) right after the unpacking.

This is work/trauma from https://github.com/Ozzyboshi/TRAUMA-FirstDemo:
a relocatable rebuild with its screens in a BSS_C hunk, the OS calls
made in user mode, VBR-aware vectors, AGA display registers reset, and
CPU-independent delays. It asks the OS for its memory: 22 KB of any
memory plus 128 + 24 + 64 KB of chip RAM, so that it still loads when
the chip RAM is fragmented (no fast RAM and hard disks mounted).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
